# Deployment and environments

## Local development

- Dependencies: Node >= 24.14.0, PNPM 10+, MySQL 8, Redis
- docker-compose.yaml provisions MySQL 8.0.43 (localhost:3309) and Redis (localhost:6380)
- app/package.json scripts:
  - pnpm dev — Nuxt dev server
  - prisma generate/migrate deploy — client and migrations
  - test, lint, e2e commands
- AGENTS.md: In Cursor Cloud, override any injected DATABASE_URL with your .env value before running prisma or dev. MySQL/Redis may need manual startup.

## Docker images

- app/Dockerfile
  - Multi-stage, runs pnpm prisma generate with placeholder DATABASE_URL at build
  - Final runner: node:24-alpine, runs .output/server/index.mjs as non-root (uid 1001), PORT env (default 3000 in Dockerfile, set to 80 in K8S)
- microservice/Dockerfile
  - Multi-stage with pnpm prisma generate
  - Final runner with PNPM; CMD switches between start/test-start based on NODE_ENV
  - Alternate target runner-keyrotate adds kubectl + jq and a key-rotation script for CronJob usage

## CI/CD (GitHub Actions)

- .github/workflows/pr.yml (PR checks)
  - Jobs: lint, test (Vitest; generates Prisma client), pre-commit security (TruffleHog and hooks), CodeQL
  - For first-party PRs: build app and microservice images tagged pr-<number>-<sha> and deploy to staging via .deploy templates
  - Verifies rollout and health via /health/ready
  - Optional: requests Cursor Bugbot comment
- .github/workflows/main.yml (main/master)
  - Builds images tagged latest and <sha>
  - Deploys to production GKE using .deploy/dineros.template.yaml and verify script
- .github/actions/build-push-gcr — composite action for docker buildx + push to gcr.io
- .github/actions/deploy-dineros-gke — renders K8S manifests via envsubst and kubectl apply

## Kubernetes manifests (.deploy/*.template.yaml)

- Namespace, Deployments for main and microservice, Services, Ingress
- Main container PORT is 80; readiness/liveness at /health/ready and /health/live
- Microservice Service exposes port 3050
- Secrets handling:
  - SECRET_DB: only field-encryption materials (DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY and optional DB_DECRYPTION_KEY_*). Do not store DATABASE_URL here
  - SECRET_DATABASE_MAIN and SECRET_DATABASE_MICRO: contain DATABASE_URL for main and microservice respectively
  - SECRET_APP: app secrets (POSTMARK, PLAID, INTERNAL_API_TOKEN, etc.)
  - SECRET_JWT: DINEROS_JWT_SECRET
  - SECRET_GA: Google service account JSON mounted at /etc/google-service-account/service-account.json

## Key rotation (staging)

- .deploy/key-rotation-cronjob.template.yaml builds a CronJob using the microservice keyrotate image to:
  - rotate DB encryption keys in the SECRET_DB secret
  - patch main/microservice Deployments for rolling restart
  - call microservice /migrate endpoint
- .deploy/key-rotation-rbac.template.yaml grants Role/RoleBinding for secrets and deployments patch/list/watch — requires IAM allowing Role/RoleBinding creation when applying

## Health checks

- App exposes GET /health/ready and /health/live (app/server/routes/health/*.ts)
- Deploy scripts verify rollout and HTTP 200 on /health/ready
